IO-33: keep [FILES] and [REPORT] keyword indices in an int

iface_readFileParams() and report_readOptions() stored findmatch()'s result
in a plain char, through a (char) cast, and tested it with k < 0. Where plain
char is unsigned (Linux on ARM and aarch64, PowerPC, s390x), findmatch()'s
-1 for an unknown word becomes 255 and the test never fires: a misspelt
[FILES] mode (SVAE HOTSTART ...) was dropped without a message and a
misspelt [REPORT] keyword was reported against its value (ERROR 205 YES).
k is now an int and the cast is gone, so an unknown word is ERROR 205 on
every platform. Nothing changes where char is signed (x86, Windows, macOS).

Requires: IO-31

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-33_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/iface.c b/src/legacy/engine/iface.c
index 23272de..600699f 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/iface.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/iface.c
@@ -76,14 +76,14 @@ int iface_readFileParams(char* tok[], int ntoks)
 //  USE/SAVE  FileType  FileName
 //
 {
-    char  k;
+    int   k;
     int   i, j;
     char  fname[MAXFNAME+1];
     double saveDateTime = 0, saveDate, saveTime;
 
     // --- determine file disposition and type
     if ( ntoks < 2 ) return error_setInpError(ERR_ITEMS, "");
-    k = (char)findmatch(tok[0], FileModeWords);
+    k = findmatch(tok[0], FileModeWords);
     if ( k < 0 ) return error_setInpError(ERR_KEYWORD, tok[0]);
     j = findmatch(tok[1], FileTypeWords);
     if ( j < 0 ) return error_setInpError(ERR_KEYWORD, tok[1]);
